course: dictionary
lesson: 15931
title: Unrecorded: when nothing was written down
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unrecorded means not written down, filmed or saved, so there is no record of it. The prefix un- means not, and recorded means saved in some way. «The lives of many ordinary people were unrecorded, so we know very little about them.» The clue is so: because nobody wrote them down, we have few facts.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «The band's first song was unrecorded, so no copy exists today.» The clues are no copy exists today. Unrecorded music has never been put onto a record, tape or file, so nobody can play it again.
explain: Unrecorded can also mean something that was never noted. «Sam forgot to write down his results, so they are unrecorded.» Sam's results still happened, but there is no written record of them. In science, that is a problem, because lost evidence cannot be checked.
fact: Unrecorded means not written down, filmed or saved.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so unrecorded is the opposite of recorded.
fact: «Unrecorded history» means the past that was never written down, especially the lives of ordinary people.
fact: Historians use objects and oral history, which means spoken memories passed down, to learn about unrecorded history.
fact: In science, always write down your results, so they are not lost.
exercise: «The lives of many ordinary people were unrecorded.» What does unrecorded mean here? | *Not written down, so no record exists | Very famous and loved by everyone | Read out loud every single day | Written in gold ink
exercise: «Sam forgot to write down his results, so they are unrecorded.» What does this tell you? | The results were filmed on a phone | Sam wrote them down twice | *Nobody wrote the results down | The results were very long
exercise: Historians learn about unrecorded history from what? | Only from the internet | Guessing, with no evidence at all | Only from the weather reports | *Old objects and spoken memories
test: «The band's first song was unrecorded, so no copy exists today.» What does unrecorded mean? | Never saved on a record, tape or file | Sung by a famous singer | *Never saved on a record, tape or file, so nobody can play it | Played very loudly
test: What is the opposite of unrecorded? | Forgotten | Ancient | *Recorded | Curt
exam: Why must a scientist write down every result, so that none are unrecorded? | So the results can be hidden from others | Because the paper looks neater | Because pens are expensive | *So the evidence is saved and can be checked later
